<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Deliberately invisible splash icon (2026-04-22 round 6).

  On Android 12+ the system SplashScreen API ALWAYS renders an icon
  during cold-start. If `windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon` is omitted
  from the theme, the platform falls back to the launcher icon with
  its default adaptive-icon treatment (white disc bubble behind the
  icon foreground). Nasser saw that fallback and reported it as
  "intro showing first, can't you avoid showing this?" — i.e. he
  wants the cold-start canvas to be visually empty, not branded with
  a mini-logo.

  The Android SplashScreen API has NO official "no icon" mode — the
  only way to suppress it is to supply an icon that matches the
  background. This vector is a solid-cream 288dp square (the adaptive
  icon size spec for splash icons). Paired with
  `windowSplashScreenIconBackgroundColor = #F5F5DC` in themes.xml,
  the rendered splash becomes: cream square masked to a cream circle
  on a cream screen = invisible.

  Do NOT replace this drawable with something visible (logo,
  monogram, etc.) unless explicitly asked — the invisibility is the
  point. The branded intro lives in Stage 2 (WarattilSplashScreen.kt).

  Size is 288dp to match the adaptive-icon splash spec; the exact
  value doesn't matter visually (the whole thing is cream-on-cream)
  but using the spec-correct size avoids subtle scaling artifacts
  on some OEM builds.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="288dp"
    android:height="288dp"
    android:viewportWidth="288"
    android:viewportHeight="288">
    <path
        android:fillColor="#F5F5DC"
        android:pathData="M0,0h288v288h-288z" />
</vector>
